2.0  Getting Started

2.1  Installing on Your Hard Drive

To install on hard drive it  is recommended a new sub-directory be  created
within the BBS directory which contains all the files relevant to The Lords
of Irongate. Assuming  your BBS  is currently on  the DH0:  drive, you  can
accomplish this installation by typing the following commands from DOS:

  CD DH0:
  MAKEDIR IRONGATE

Then if installing from a registered floppy:

  COPY DF0:#? DH0:IRONGATE

NOTE: It is  NOT necessary to  copy any  of the files  within the  DF0:DEMO
subdirectory. That subdirectory contains  an LHA file  which is a  complete
working 'freely distributable'  demo. It  is totally  independent from  the
actual registered version and was placed on the disk to allow you to give a
copy to  family or  friends for  their evaluation  (without affecting  your
license agreement). DO  NOT distribute  copies of the  disk itself  though,
make a copy of the file(s) within the DEMO subdirectory ONLY!


2.2  Command line options

Irongate has a  number of arguments  which can be  specif ied to change  its
mode of operation, to see a quick help screen of syntax and synopsis of the
available arguments, from DOS type:

  IRONGATE     or      IRONGATE /H


The complete list of command line syntax is as follows:


  IRONGATE  [SYSPW=yyy] [MAXMOVES=xxx] [USERNAME=zzz]
            [ANSI=MONO] or [ANSI=COLOR]


The argument description is as follows:
  -------------------- OPTIONAL ---------------------------------

  SYSPW=yyy      ->Set System Password to yyy. This password has
                   absolutely nothing to do with the BBS, it is
                   strictly for use with IRONGATE and allows you
                   to delete players from the players file (each
                   player can delete his own character but only
                   the one who knows the sysop password can
                   delete all or any other player).

  MAXMOVES=xxx   ->Set the maximum nr of player moves per day to
                   xxx. Since this is not a strategy game I
                   recommend this be set to a high number such as
                   5000 (The movements go by quickly!)
                   This would allow each player about 5-15
                   minutes a day of play time to get high score



                   or complete the quest...

  USERNAME=zzz   ->This sets the players name to the same as the
                   passed argument zzz which should be the BBS
                   Username. Assuming the username is no longer
                   than 19 characters). If you configure your
                   BBS with this you accomplish two things:
                   (1) You ensure no user has more than 1 player
                       at the game at one time, and
                   (2) You prevent any other user from using an
                       alternate account to hack into someones
                       game play.
                   Also, the entry prompt for password is
                   redundant and will not exist if you specify to
                   use this USERNAME argument.

  ANSI=MONO or   ->Sets the text mode of operation to limit or not
  ANSI=COLOR       limit ANSI COLOR codes. Default is ANSI=COLOR


2.3  Configuring The Program to Run from your BBS

To configure  IRONGATE to  run from  your BBS  you must  remember to  first
ASSIGN IRONGATE: to the  location of the irongate  files. You can then  run
Irongate by simply  specifying to  run the door  (as a  dos executable)  by
adding the door  as a  menu command which  will execute  Irongate with  the
arguments you with to have decided to pass. The following are some  example
methods to run irongate:

(A) ;This example assumes your BBS will pass a variable %ANSI as
    ;either COLOR or MONO (Note: IRONGATE will ALWAYS need ANSI
    ;screen positioning codes, but color or mono is optional).

    IRONGATE:IRONGATE ANSI=%ANSI

(B) ;This example will both set the system password to FRODO in
    ;order that you may delete outdated characters, and it will
    ;limit the player to one play a day of no more than 3000 moves.

    IRONGATE:IRONGATE MAXMOVES=3000 SYSPW=FRODO

(C) ;This example will always start the game in MONO mode
    ; (no color)

    IRONGATE:IRONGATE ANSI=MONO

An optional method of running irongate  includes using a script file  (also
known as a BATCH  file) which can  be called out from  some BBS systems  in
lieu of the executable. The script file  can then in turn do your  assign:,
change the current directory, run the  program, and even copy the  hiscores
files to your BBS message/bulletins area for display. Most BBS do not allow
the use of these script files, but  if yours do es there is a sample script
enclosed called: LOISTART which can be edited to suit your needs.




